# The tutorial from the journey to the city to the closing frame, re-shot on its own from rest.cli's
# checkpoint taken on returning to the world map after the job menu (build/rec_rest/saves/03_job_menu.json,
# copied to the --save-path before the take). Its lines are rest.cli's from "Travel to the city" on; a fight
# re-rolls on every load, so a lost fight is re-shot by running this again.
#
# FLAGS: as rest.cli's.
allow-flag-miss --start-area
allow-flag-miss --observe-only

wait mode MainMenu 900
mark resume_city
click menu Continue
wait mode WorldView 900
cursor rest
hold 2

# ── Travel to the city ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mark travel_city
clip travel_city
travel 27788
wait 900
cursor rest
hold 4
travel-go
wait mode EncounterPrompt 900
clip end travel_city

# ── The second fight ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Another wolf, already beside us and slower than we are: five snap thrusts, our turns ended between.
mark fight_2
clip fight_2
cursor rest
hold 4
click engage
wait mode Fighting 900
cursor rest
hold 5
regions
# A turn of ours, if the fight is still on: wait for the fight to need us; meet up to four of the enemy's
# blows (each a dice box waiting for Continue), spending humors on our defence while the blow would land;
# then thrust, spend humors only while the roll falls short, and end the turn.
skip-unless fighting 69
wait turn 900
skip-unless dice 10
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
click humor spleen needed
click die needed
click humor pulmones needed
click die needed
click humor paunch needed
click die needed
hold 1
click continue
wait turn 900
skip-unless dice 10
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
click humor spleen needed
click die needed
click humor pulmones needed
click die needed
click humor paunch needed
click die needed
hold 1
click continue
wait turn 900
skip-unless dice 10
click humor hepar needed
click die needed
click humor spleen needed
